config BR2_PACKAGE_ARTLYNK_P1_VENDOR_FIRMWARE
	bool "artlynk-p1-vendor-firmware"
	help
	  Extracts the proprietary blobs the BetaFPV P1 SKY needs from
	  BetaFPV's stock P1 SKY OTA image into output/images/artlynk-p1/
	  and installs the codec/ISP ones:
	    /lib/firmware/cnm/wave521c_k3_codec_fw.bin   (wave5 codec)
	    /lib/firmware/artosyn/nt99235-tuning-preview-fpv.bin (ISP)
	    /lib/firmware/ar8030/bb_config_air.json      (P1 RF config)
	  The AR8030 baseband image and the generated p1_ascent_air.json
	  (P1 as AP, Ascent link settings) are installed by the ar8030
	  package, as ar8030.img and ar8030.json, through the device's
	  fetch script. The stock SPL/U-Boot/DDR
	  firmware are kept in output/images/artlynk-p1/ for USB boot.

	  Nothing is committed. A local stock image is used first
	  (ARTLYNK_P1_VENDOR_IMG, else cache/vendor-images/P1_SKY_*.img);
	  without one, BetaFPV's v2.0.5 image is downloaded from Google
	  Drive into cache/vendor-images/ by the device's
	  scripts/fetch-vendor-img.sh (file id in the .mk). See extract.py for host prerequisites. Missing pieces
	  are skipped with a warning, never a build failure.
